spans.s:
saúbhaga, n. [subhaga] V.: welfare, 🞄good fortune, happiness, enjoyment (pl. gifts 🞄of fortune, joys);
 P.: beauty, loveliness, grace;
 🞄-tvá, n. welfare, happiness (RV.).

saúbhāg-ya, n. [subhaga] welfare, 🞄luck, good fortune;
 popularity;
 conjugal felicity;
 🞄beauty, charm (of persons and things): 🞄-vat, a. endowed with beauty.
